                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Pixel Stories of Dungeon is a turnbased roguelite rpg game. You are a small child that wants to be the next hero in the tournament. Therefore you have to defeat different bosses in all parts/dungeons in the world.\nYou can go to these parts of the world by selecting them on the world map. All these dungeons have many monsters which you must/can defeat. Each dungeon has a few stages before you meet up the boss.\nAfter that you will return to town. You cannot leave a dungeon.\nLike most games of this genre you can regain health by walking around.\n\nYou can catch monsters as a pet (like Pokemon). Only one monster can help you fight in every battle. Your pet can die. If that happens, you have to catch a new one. You can control what your pet will do in the game.\nYour mother will build a place for your pets. Here you can store a few pets. You have to bring food for them, so they level up.\nThe monsters in the game only move when you move. Game is fully turnbased.\nLike most games in this genre you have to grind to level up.\n\nThere a lot of items you can buy, find and sell.\n\nThis game has no permadeath. If you die you will be rescued by the citadel. You can keep your items, but it will cost you some gold.\n\nThe game is fully played with a keyboard, you can assign the keys you would like to use.\nYou can only save at a save point in town.\n\nThe graphics are okay, if you don't mind pixel art like me. Sounds are okay too.\n\nOne thing I really missed in this game is a running option to speed up some gameplay.\nI wish the game will have controller support in the future. Also a save anytime option would be nice.\nThe dev told me this game will have achievements soon/, which would be nice.\nThe dev is very active on the forum, to help you with all questions, I like that a lot.\n\nThe game is fun to play, if you like pixel art rpg/roguelites.\n\nThe game has enough content to justify it's price tag.\n\nI would give it a 7.5 out of 10\n\n\n[url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/32732116-IndieGems/] More reviews on our Curator Page [/url]",
